---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import InflationCalculator from '../../components/InflationCalculator';
---

<Layout
  title="Inflation Calculator"
  description="Free calculator showing how inflation erodes purchasing power over time, and how much you'd need in the future to match today's buying power."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand">Tool<span class="text-orange">/</span></p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-paper sm:text-4xl">Inflation Calculator</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted">
      See how much purchasing power an amount of money loses over time, and what you'd need in the future to
      keep up.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <InflationCalculator client:load />
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-10 max-w-none prose-a:text-brand">
      <h2>How this calculator works</h2>
      <p>
        Inflation means prices generally rise over time, so the same amount of money buys less in the future
        than it does today. This tool applies a constant annual inflation rate to your amount over your chosen
        number of years, showing both the future dollar cost of today's basket of goods and the real purchasing
        power your money would lose if left unspent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read our full <a href="/blog/what-is-inflation/">inflation guide</a> for the reasoning behind this, and
        our <a href="/blog/lifestyle-inflation/">guide to lifestyle inflation</a> for a related but different
        concept — spending more as your income grows.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
